Z||000001||RNGCRSH||01-03-2001||11:30 PM||||Sounds like the TC lockup solenoid is engaged.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||01-03-2001||11:32 PM||||A bad TCC switch (torque convertor clutch) will cause it to die.  I had one go bad on me while I was driving.....it just died.<P>A simple way to test it is to unplug it.  If the stalling goes away, then your switch is to blame.  Look on the drivers side of the engine compartment towards the firewall.......you will see a square 4 prong plug attached to the tranny.  This in the TCC switch.  Unplug it and drive it around.<P><BR>As for your engine knocking.....if it is always present (at all RPM's) then it is likely a spun bearing.  Considering the shape of the oil you drained this isn't far fetched.<P>Good luck.   ||||reg||1
Z||000003||TheFiero64||01-04-2001||11:11 AM||||My 84 SE was acting like that and come to find out one of the wires on the coil fell out and the other 3 were corroded. The coil could also be bad. The stalling in gear prob. is the tcc relay. Unplug it and see if it runs fine.||||reg||1
